<LegalPage
	title="Cookie Policy"
	description="How LockDraft uses cookies and similar browser technologies."
>
	<h2>What cookies are</h2>
	<p>
		Cookies are small text files stored by a website in your browser. Similar
		technologies include local storage and pixels.
	</p>

	<h2>How LockDraft uses them</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Essential:</strong> preferences and functions required for the site to work.</li>
		<li><strong>Analytics:</strong> aggregate measurement of visits and content performance, when enabled.</li>
		<li><strong>Advertising:</strong> ad delivery, frequency measurement, and personalisation, when enabled and permitted.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Your choices</h2>
	<p>
		You can block or remove cookies through your browser settings. Blocking
		essential storage may affect site functionality. When optional technologies
		are enabled, the site will provide the applicable consent and preference
		controls.
	</p>

	<h2>Questions</h2>
	<p>
		Email <a href="mailto:hello@lockdraft.com">hello@lockdraft.com</a> if you
		have a question about cookies used on the site.
	</p>
</LegalPage>
